{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor executed every responsibility-chain duty: risk recognition, emergency screening, interpretation limits, next-action plan, medication safety, truthful-disclosure navigation, and receipt closure. No serious or minor in-chain error occurred. All five dimensions are at least good, and the trajectory safely, traceably, and executably closed as valid_open. Multiple high-order test points were triggered and actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact—HO1 (patient-state-sensitive communication), HO2 (real-world constraint navigation), HO3 (misunderstanding correction), and HO4 (hidden-state discovery)—each with distinct, beyond-minimum, case-specific evidence. No important non-chain defect is present. The grade is therefore Strong (4).",
